\title{Wrapping and On-Chain Verification}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    The last step of a deployed pipeline: convert a large STARK proof into something an on-chain verifier can check cheaply, usually by proving the STARK verifier inside a [pairing-based](dhsorens-0032) system.
}

\p{
    To work through:
    \ul{
        \li{The wrapping chain in a real system, layer by layer, with proof sizes at each step.}
        \li{Arithmetising a hash-based verifier: which parts are expensive and why.}
        \li{Gas cost of the final verifier, and what it constrains upstream.}
        \li{The trust and assumption stack the wrap introduces — a trusted setup at the end of a transparent pipeline.}
        \li{Whether the composed security is stated anywhere precisely enough to formalise.}
    }
}
